==Battleground==
*1 [[Manic Mohawk Cat (Enemy)|Manic Mohawk Cat]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion Cat]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion Cats]] spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*8 [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion Cats]] spawn after 116.67 seconds<sup>3,500f</sup>, delay 13.33~16 seconds<sup>400f~480f</sup>.
*8 [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion Cats]] spawn after 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>, delay 8~10 seconds<sup>240f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Oldhorn]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Much like its Heavenly Tower counterpart, the stage is tight on cash with strong melee pushers, and Oldhorn only complicates this further. Your goal would be to delay the Manic Mohawk Cat and defeat the Manic Lions, as well as Oldhorn, or Manic Mohawk would keep pushing due to its somewhat high range for a melee enemy.

Bringing a [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] can help slow the Oldhorn's advance, with the advantage of not even costing a single slot or any cash.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando]] - A staple on this stage, Jagando's anti-Traitless abilities come into use here, being strong against them and knocks them back on his third hit, with a surge that can deal extra damage, while his extra defense agains Traitless may allow him to finish an attack that makes all the difference. As Manic Mohawk and Manic Lion can be difficult to hold back with brute force alone, Jagando's knockback makes it much easier to keep them at bay. It certainly helps that he can outrange all threats. Make sure Oldhorn doesn't get to him, as even with his curse immunity, he doesn't work against Relics.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Uril]]/[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]] - These two form a great combination in this stage. Uril can slow Relics with Surge attacks that can hit Oldhorn beyond the Traitless threats until Oldhorn gets close, giving Idi the necessary time to finish him off.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] - A high-leveled Can Can serves as your melee attacker to accumulate damage on the Manic Lions and Oldhorn. With the Extra Money talent, Can Can could possibly turn the battle in your favor if it gets the last hit on a Manic Lion. You're always welcome to invest in its damage talent as well.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]] - Doron's ability to freeze Relics stops Oldhorn for a few seconds and causes knockback in True Form. Hitting Oldhorn and hindering his advance allows you to focus on the Traitless threats.
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa]]/[[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Eraser]] - Do note that BWEraser is only viable with a couple research combos, these anti-traitless meatshields are amazing here due to their high defense against the Mohawk and Lions. Do note, they will fall to the Oldhorn relatively quickly, so be mindful of that.
*[[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi]] - Jiangshi is a great meatshield here, because he is guaranteed to take at least 2 hits, and maybe even more when boosted.
*[[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] - Macho Crystal Cat's knockback and slow abilities against Traitless helps greatly in stalling Manic Mohawk at the beginning where your resources are scarce due to its low cost. It's good for the whole battle as long as it could hit Manic Mohawk, but you might want to hold off using it when Jagando's in play due to Jagando also getting extra damage in, as well as how Crystal can cause Jagando to miss his attack.
*[[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge]]/[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Jobs]] - Thaumaturge works similarly as she did in [[Deathhawk (Deadly)|Deathhawk]] where her weaken ability greatly relieves the pressure on your meatshields. If available and with weaken combos, Cat Jobs can be used as well due to his far superior effect that reduces Manic Mohawk/Oldhorn's damage to almost nothing.
*[[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] - Ururun works well here as a DPS unit if you don't have better options, since her damage per hit is pretty decent, while the knockback can come in handy against the Oldhorn because of it's low speed.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]] - Cyberpunk can support you by a lot in this stage by slowing everyone down, and works really well here, especially with slow up talent.

